# Never ship host node_modules into the image — pnpm symlinks point at host paths
# (e.g. C:/Users/.../.pnpm/...) which are invalid inside the container. The
# Dockerfile runs `pnpm install` against the manifests; let it create fresh
# symlinks rather than copying the host's.
**/node_modules

# Build / dev artifacts
**/dist
**/out
**/.vite
**/coverage
**/.turbo

# VCS + tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.beads
.husky
.vscode
.idea

# Logs / local files
**/*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Desktop / platform-specific (server image doesn't need them)
desktop
deploy
docs
oss-sync
tools
scripts
e2e

# OS noise
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
